---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Eyebrow from "../../components/Eyebrow.astro";
import Prose from "../../components/Prose.astro";
import { site } from "../../site.config";

/*
 * Written against what the app actually stores, not from a template. Every row
 * of the table below maps to a real table in the SupplyO backend. If the schema
 * gains a new kind of personal data, this page changes in the same commit.
 *
 * Deliberately absent, because SupplyO does none of them: cookies and web
 * tracking, IP/device fingerprinting for analytics, marketing or newsletters,
 * social sign-on, vouchers, GPS location, and payment card data. Claiming any of
 * them would also contradict the Play Data safety declaration, and a policy that
 * disagrees with that form is a rejection.
 */
const updated = "2 September 2026";
---
<Base
  brand="supplyo"
  title="SupplyO — Privacy Policy"
  description="How SupplyO collects, uses and shares personal information, where it is held, and how to access, correct or delete it."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-16 md:pt-20">
    <Eyebrow text="Legal" />
    <h1 class="display-wide mt-8 text-4xl text-ink sm:text-5xl">SupplyO Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 font-mono text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <Prose>
      <p>
        SupplyO is operated by <strong>{site.legalName}</strong>, a business
        registered in {site.country}. This policy explains what the SupplyO mobile
        app collects, why, where it is held, and who else can see it. It applies to
        both people who use SupplyO: the <strong>supplier</strong> who runs a
        delivery business, and the <strong>customer</strong> who orders from him.
      </p>
      <p>
        By creating an account and using SupplyO, you accept this policy. If you do
        not agree with it, please do not use the app.
      </p>

      <h2>The most important thing to know</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Your supplier can see your information.</strong> When you order
        from a supplier on SupplyO, that supplier sees your name, phone number,
        delivery address, what you ordered, what was delivered to you, and what
        you have paid and still owe. That is the app working as intended, since it is
        how he knows where to deliver and what to charge, but you should know it
        before you place an order. A supplier only ever sees his own customers.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Your supplier is responsible for how he uses it.</strong> He is an
        independent business, not our staff. We decide what SupplyO collects and
        how the app handles it. What he does with what he sees, how he keeps it and
        who in his shop he shows it to, is his own responsibility under the law.
        If a supplier misuses your information, tell us at
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>: we can remove his access
        to the platform, though we cannot reach into his own records.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Information</th><th>Why we hold it</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Your name</td><td>So your supplier knows whose order and whose bill this is.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Your phone number</td><td>It is how you sign in, and how your supplier calls you about an order.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Your delivery address and area</td><td>So the supplier can deliver, and so you can find suppliers who cover your area.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Your orders and deliveries</td><td>Products, quantities, dates and prices: the record of what was asked for and what arrived.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Bills and payments</td><td>What was charged, what was paid, and what is still owed.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Notification token</td><td>An identifier from Google that lets us send your phone a notification when your order is answered.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Sign-in records</td><td>Session tokens and failed sign-in attempts, so we can keep your account secure.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        We do <strong>not</strong> collect your device's GPS location, your
        contacts, your photos, or anything from other apps on your phone. Your
        delivery address is what you typed, not where your phone is. SupplyO has
        <strong>no cookies, no web tracking, no advertising and no analytics</strong>,
        and <strong>we never handle your money</strong>. You pay your supplier
        directly, so we hold no card or bank details at all.
      </p>

      <h3>Information about other people</h3>
      <p>
        If you give us someone else's details, such as a delivery address for a relative,
        or, if you are a supplier, your customers' names and numbers entered into
        the app, you confirm you are entitled to share them with us, and you
        should tell that person their information is in SupplyO.
      </p>

      <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your supplier</strong>, as described above.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Google</strong>. SupplyO runs on Google Cloud and uses Firebase
          Cloud Messaging to deliver notifications. Your information is stored on
          Google's servers, which may be outside Pakistan, and your notification
          token and the contents of a notification pass through them.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Courts and authorities</strong>. If we are lawfully required to
          disclose information by a court, regulator or other competent authority,
          we will comply.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        That is the complete list. <strong>We do not sell or rent your
        information</strong> to anyone, for any purpose.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>See what we hold.</strong> Ask us and we will tell you what
          information is stored about you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Correct it.</strong> You can change your own name and address in
          the app at any time. Your phone number is how you sign in, so it cannot
          be edited in the app. Write to us and we will change it for you.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Delete your account.</strong> See
          <a href="/supplyo/delete-account">the deletion request page</a>, and read
          the next section, which explains what deletion does and does not remove.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Any of these: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. We respond
        within {site.deletionResponseDays} days, free of charge.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it, and what deletion means</h2>
      <p>
        We want to be straight about this rather than promise something the app
        does not do.
      </p>
      <p>
        Orders, deliveries, bills and payments are a <strong>business record shared
        between you and your supplier</strong>. When you ask us to delete your
        account, we deactivate it and remove your personal details, meaning your name,
        phone number and address, so you can no longer be identified from them or
        signed in. <strong>The underlying delivery and payment records are
        retained</strong>, no longer linked to your personal details, because they
        are also your supplier's record of goods he sold and money he is owed, and
        Pakistani tax law requires a business to keep its accounting records for
        several years.
      </p>

      <h2>How it is protected</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Everything between the app and our servers travels over HTTPS.</li>
        <li>Passwords are stored only as a one-way hash, so nobody at {site.company} can read your password.</li>
        <li>Sign-in tokens are held in your phone's own encrypted storage.</li>
        <li>Sign-in attempts are rate-limited to make guessing a password impractical.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        No system is perfectly secure, and information sent over the internet can
        never be guaranteed against every attack. We will not ask you for your
        password by phone, SMS or email. If anyone does, it is not us, and we
        would like to hear about it.
      </p>

      <h2>If the business changes hands</h2>
      <p>
        If {site.legalName} is sold or merges with another company, the information
        described here may transfer to the new owner, who would be bound by this
        policy until you are told otherwise.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        SupplyO is a tool for running a delivery business and is not directed at
        children. We do not knowingly create accounts for anyone under 18.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we change what we collect or who we share it with, we will update this
        page and change the date at the top.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy, or about your information, go to
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.
        {site.address && <> Our postal address is {site.address}.</>}
        See also our <a href="/supplyo/terms">terms of use</a>.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </div>
</Base>
